{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ruinable-priggish-silverfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\\n\\nRunning review-code in a clean worktree with the project-owned review-phase-boundaries prompt present fails before reviewing the diff. Both attested and local source modes report unknown prompt code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries while listing only built-ins. Offline project-prompt tests pass and the file exists at .rebar/prompts/code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries.md.\\n\\n## Plan\\n\\n- Reproduce review-code prompt discovery through the real CLI in a temporary repository/worktree.\\n- Trace repo_root propagation into project criteria routing and prompt loading.\\n- Make project-owned code-review prompts resolve consistently in attested and local source modes without changing built-in prompt behavior.\\n- Add a behavioral CLI regression test that runs review-code far enough to select the project prompt, using a fake runner to avoid a live model call.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] review-code resolves an activated project-owned code-review prompt from .rebar/prompts.\\n- [ ] Both attested and local source modes use the same project prompt registry semantics.\\n- [ ] Unknown project prompt identifiers still fail closed with a clear error.\\n- [ ] A behavioral regression test exercises public review-code dispatch without source-text grep assertions.\\n- [ ] make lint, make typecheck, and make test pass.","id":"6ba6-ae90-28a6-4394","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["code-review","prompt-registry"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-code cannot resolve active project prompt from .rebar/prompts"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785218223206211001,"uuid":"3a27aa83-7b3d-4bd4-8141-e9205edcc912"}